course: dictionary
lesson: 15005
title: Feelings that hide
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some feelings are not shouted out loud. They sit quietly inside and change how you act. Resentful is one of these words. It describes feeling angry and bitter because you think you were treated unfairly. «Mia was resentful when her brother got the bigger slice of cake.» Mia thinks the sharing was not fair, so she feels bitter about it.
explain: Read the clues around the word. Why was Mia resentful? Because the bigger slice went to her brother, and she felt she should have had it. The reason in the sentence is the clue. Check it: could you swap in angry? Angry fits a little, but resentful is more exact, because the anger has built up over something that feels unfair.
explain: Resentful can also describe a look or words that show this feeling. «He gave her a resentful look across the classroom.» Nobody says the feeling out loud, but the look shows it. Phrases help too: you can feel resentful of someone, or resentful about something.
fact: Resentful means feeling angry and bitter because you think you were treated unfairly.
fact: Resentful can also describe a look or words that show that feeling.
fact: Resentful is an adjective. Its forms are more resentful and most resentful.
fact: Useful phrases: «resentful of» a person, «resentful about» a thing, or «feel resentful».
fact: Angry is a general word; resentful is about anger that grows from feeling treated unfairly.
exercise: «Mia was resentful when her brother got the bigger slice of cake.» Why was Mia resentful? | She had lost her cake | She had been given a present | She was very tired | *She thought the sharing was unfair
exercise: «He gave her a resentful look across the classroom.» What does resentful show here? | Hunger | Sleepy tiredness | Happy surprise | *Bitter anger about being treated unfairly
exercise: Which word fits best? Sam feels ___ of his sister, who always gets to choose the film. | Happy | Curious | Brave | *Resentful
test: «After being left out of the game, Priya felt resentful.» What does resentful mean here? | Hungry for lunch | Calm and sleepy | Excited about the next game | *Angry and bitter, because she thought it was unfair
test: Which sentence uses resentful correctly? | Tom was resentful of the sunny weather | Tom was resentful with a big smile | *Tom was resentful about being blamed for the broken vase | Tom was resentful and eating a sandwich
exam: Which sentence shows someone is resentful? | Tom laughed and cheered when his team won | Tom ate his lunch quickly and went outside | Tom hummed a happy tune while he read his book | *Tom muttered that it was not fair he had to tidy up alone, and he glared at his brother
